# P Spot — Cursor Rules
# Keep this file in the root of the p-spot/ directory.
# This is the source of truth for every technical and product decision.
# Do not deviate from anything defined here without explicit instruction.

---

## PRODUCT OVERVIEW

P Spot is a mobile app where users photograph and score their most epic outdoor pee spots.
An AI evaluates each photo and generates a score. Scores compete on global leaderboards,
appear on a live map, and feed into a social feed called The Stream.

Companion app in development: DrinkSpot (drinkspot.app) — same concept, different liquid.

---

## TECH STACK — NON-NEGOTIABLE

| Layer              | Technology                                      |
|--------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| Mobile app         | React Native + Expo (managed workflow)           |
| Backend / Database | Supabase (auth, PostgreSQL, storage, realtime)   |
| AI scoring/mod     | Claude API — claude-sonnet-4-20250514 (vision)   |
| Maps               | Mapbox                                           |
| Image storage      | Supabase Storage                                 |
| EXIF parsing       | exifr (client-side, before upload)               |
| Auth               | Supabase Auth (email, Apple, Google)             |
| Ads                | Google AdMob                                     |
| Analytics          | PostHog                                          |
| Push notifications | Expo Push Notifications + Supabase triggers      |
| Strava             | Strava API (OAuth, activity matching)            |
| Age verification   | DOB + checkbox at V1. Persona at V2.             |
| Landing page       | Static HTML — index.html (already built)         |
| Landing backend    | Same Supabase project as the app                 |

Do NOT suggest alternatives to these. Do NOT introduce additional dependencies
without being explicitly asked.

