## DESIGN SYSTEM

### Typefaces
- Headings / display: Syne (weight 700, 800)
- Body / UI:          Inter (weight 400, 500)

### Color palette
- Primary yellow:   #D4B84A  (hydrated pee yellow — the brand color)
- Yellow light:     #F5EEC8
- Yellow mid:       #B89A2E
- Yellow deep:      #7A6318
- Yellow text:      #3D3010
- Map background:   #EDE9C8

Always use CSS variables. Never hardcode hex values inline.

### Tone
- Dry, confident, self-aware humor
- Never try-hard or cringe
- Short copy. Punchy.
- Examples: "Stay hydrated." / "Locked in." / "Rate the view. Claim the spot."

---

## IMAGE MODERATION + SCORING (Claude API)

Every submission makes ONE Claude API call that handles BOTH moderation and scoring.
Never make two separate calls.

Model: claude-sonnet-4-20250514
Input: base64 image + structured prompt
Output: JSON with moderation result + full score breakdown

If moderation fails → reject, do not score, increment user strike count.
Strike thresholds: 1 = warning, 2 = 7-day ban, 3 = permanent ban.

EXIF GPS data is required. If absent → reject with message:
"Original photo required — screenshots don't count."

---

## STRAVA INTEGRATION

- User connects Strava once via OAuth in settings
- On spot submission, match nearest activity by timestamp (within 2-hour window)
- Pull: distance_mi, elevation_gain_ft, duration_sec, suffer_score, activity_type
- If no match found → skip effort bonus gracefully, do not error
- Effort bonus: scaled 0–10 pts based on distance + elevation gain

---

## AD PLACEMENT

Primary slot: AFTER submission is confirmed, WHILE the AI score is loading.
This is the highest-attention, highest-mood moment in the app.
Do not place ads anywhere else at launch.
Ad network: Google AdMob.

---

## SCREENS (complete list)

1.  Onboarding (4 slides)
2.  Sign up / Log in
3.  Age verification gate
4.  Home — map view (default) + table toggle of own recent spots
5.  The Stream — social feed from Streamers
6.  Submit flow — upload → EXIF check → privacy picker → ad → score reveal
7.  Score reveal — full breakdown, Strava strip, AI quote, share button
8.  Spot detail — Strava-style full view (tappable from map, stream, leaderboard)
9.  Leaderboard — Friends / State / Country / Continent / Global + category tabs
10. Badges & achievements — Apple Watch style, locked badges greyed with progress
11. Level progress — XP breakdown, tier roadmap
12. Profile — spot grid, stats, level, badges
13. Profile settings — account, Strava connect, notifications, privacy defaults
14. Notification center
15. Privacy picker — bottom sheet on submit: Public / Streamers / Private
16. Shared spot web view — recipient view via share link (non-app users see CTA)

---

## LEADERBOARD CATEGORIES

- Top score of all time
- Most total submissions
- Top average score (min 10 submissions)
- Longest active streak
- Most scores above 90
- Most wildlife easter eggs
- Highest danger score
- Best hydration score
- Most exotic toilet
- Weekly hot streak (most submissions in 7 days)
- Most Strava-linked submissions

---

## WHAT NOT TO DO

- Do NOT cap scores at 100
- Do NOT use streak data in individual spot scores
- Do NOT build a DM system (use native share sheet instead)
- Do NOT restrict signup by gender
- Do NOT use localStorage or sessionStorage in any web-facing code
- Do NOT introduce new dependencies without being asked
- Do NOT use "likes", "comments", "followers", or "posts" in UI copy
- Do NOT make separate API calls for moderation and scoring — one call does both
- Do NOT expose private spots on the map or leaderboard under any circumstance
- Do NOT use WidthType.PERCENTAGE in any docx generation
- Do NOT use Bebas Neue (old font — replaced by Syne)
